@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@
+# Agent Dashboard notification bridge
+
+This local branch adds `POST /notifications` so Kiro agents can publish durable inbox messages without
+spending a model call. The upstream Pizza Bot runtime remains otherwise unchanged.
+
+## Request
+
+```json
+{
+  "title": "Report ready",
+  "body": "The report was published.",
+  "source": "reporting-agent",
+  "severity": "info",
+  "requiresAction": false,
+  "idempotencyKey": "reporting-agent:report:2026-09-17",
+  "link": "http://127.0.0.1:7781/private/report"
+}
+```
+
+`severity` is `info`, `warning`, or `critical`. `link` is optional and accepts only HTTP(S).
+
+## Semantics
+
+- `idempotencyKey` maps deterministically to one notification thread;
+- a duplicate returns the existing thread without another checkpoint write;
+- routine messages go to `Agent Updates`;
+- messages requiring attention go to `Action Required` and receive an `[ACTION]` title prefix;
+- critical messages are pinned;
+- all new notifications are unread;
+- content is written directly to LangGraph state as an AI message, without an LLM invocation;
+- failed checkpoint persistence removes the empty metadata thread.
+
+The endpoint does not set Pizza Bot's native `awaitingAction`. That flag is reserved for a real
+LangGraph HITL interrupt with a resolvable decision. Kiro needs-input events remain clearly labeled
+and grouped, while true Pizza workflows continue using the native Action filter.
+
+## Validation
+
+- five route tests cover creation, dedupe, routing, validation and rollback;
+- a real loopback request produced one message and the duplicate produced no second write;
+- the rendered browser UI contained the title and body;
+- the fixture thread was removed after validation.
+
+## Embedded theme synchronization
+
+The Agent Dashboard sends `agent-dashboard-theme` with `light` or `dark` through `postMessage`.
+Pizza accepts it only from `http://127.0.0.1:7780` or `http://localhost:7780`, applies the theme and
+keeps it authoritative while embedded. A readiness message closes the iframe-load race.
+
+## Direct Kiro routing
+
+The Composer includes a `To` selector. `Pizza Bot` keeps normal DeepAgents/LangGraph behavior; an
+exact Kiro agent target calls `POST /kiro/handoffs` instead. Every explicit submit carries a new
+`requestId`: network replay of one request stays idempotent, while deliberately resending identical
+text creates a fresh handoff.
+
+```text
+Composer To=<agent>
+  -> handoff.sh with exact target + business idempotency key
+  -> agents-state queue with lease/recovery
+  -> target agent response contract
+  -> pizza-a2a-bridge.py
+  -> POST /kiro/responses
+  -> same Pizza thread becomes unread
+```
+
+The semantic response proof requires the Kiro final-answer `>` prefix and searches only the last 20
+non-empty log lines, so prompt/docs/tool output cannot satisfy it. Responses are deduplicated by
+`handoffId`. If the user deleted the thread before delivery, the API returns `orphaned=true` and does
+not recreate it; deletion during append is also covered. A redelivery is a no-op. Explicit
+`NEEDS_INPUT` returns with status `needs-input` and moves the thread to `Action Required`.
+Attachments to Kiro targets are disabled during the pilot; Pizza Bot recipients keep normal
+attachment support.
+
+`GET /kiro/agents` reads valid top-level Kiro agent JSON configs from `PIZZA_KIRO_AGENTS_DIR`
+(default `~/.kiro/agents`). KiroCrew agents remain independent and are listed only because they are
+valid agents; no KiroCrew runtime or files are modified by the bridge.
